Sval: overflow the header's controls in an order, and offer no customize mode from the overflow panel

Sval's header is one row that gives its controls up one at a time as the
window narrows: an item's overflowpriority says when it leaves, and the
panel lists what left in the row's order. The navigation buttons and
downloads can leave, so they lose `overflows="false"`, and the downloads
panel opens from the overflow button while its button is there, as it does
from the panel area. An item that appears or grows in the row resizes no
window, so the toolbar watches its items' sizes too.

Sval's header has a fixed layout and closes customize mode, so the overflow
panel's footer and its items' context menu offer no "Customize Toolbar"
item.

